  "label": "Stereotype of Economic Dependence",
  "description": "The stereotype that transgender people are 'begging' implies they are economically dependent, morally inferior, or reliant on charity or handouts. This is a harmful and false stereotype that perpetuates poverty and social exclusion. It is often used to justify discrimination and to deny transgender people access to economic opportunities and social support.",
